  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is implemented. The new tests and the existing `test_types.py`, `test_info_dict.py` and `test_basic.py` pass (177 passed, 2 skipped).\n\n- **Parsing:** `--set a=b` gives `(\"a\", \"b\")`, and the split is on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=` or with an empty key fails with `'abc' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Code:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Docs:** I added entries in `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- **Tests:** they are in `tests/test_types.py` and cover valid values and the failure cases. I didn't add an info-dict test, since that file only lists the built-in types.\n\nThe changelog is `CHANGES.md`, not `CHANGES.rst` as I'd written in the plan. 8.5.0 is already released, so I added a new \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" section there and marked the class `versionadded:: 8.6`. Rename that if the next release will have a different number.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
